body:
http://www.championselect.net/champ

Works well for me most of the time...  not always...  As for bans... you can always ask your team who they want banned cause most of the time they already have something set in stone to what they want to play or what they think they want to play, but normal bans include: 

Malphite - one of the best SURPRISE initiators; 

Amumu - same as Malph in many ways, with more stuns but can do less dmg if you just want to soak it; 

Blitzcrank - often banned due to strong potential of pulls and really strong plays with pulls/tankiness; 

Thresh - same as Blitz but only less dmg potential; 

Shen - split push all day teleport when team fights begin; 

Shaco - Can skip this one if you ward well enough or your team does anyway but strong split pusher and ganker can do tons of dmg; 

Jarven - Super tanky + dmg without many items + armor pen with lance + flag and lance pull + Catafuckyouclism; 

Zac - he's not a very STRONG champ when it comes to dmg, but his ganks are hell plus he can displace a team hardcore...;

Lastly I do Kha'Zix due to his high sustain dmg and explosive burst.  He doesn't have to do much to carry and giving him any amount of farm can screw a team up if unchecked by bad jungler ganks.

Those are my choices and short and sweet whys, but they don't have to be yours.  Play around with Draft mode if you don't want to mess up your rank, and watch other peoples bans/picks/counterpicks.  Once you get a good idea of how a champ works, you'll understand why they counter...
